## 2. Web Exploitation

| Tool / Command | What it does |
|----------------|--------------|
| Browser DevTools (`F12`) | Inspect HTML, JavaScript, cookies, storage, and network requests. |
| `curl -i http://target/` | Fetches a page and shows response headers (`-i`). |
| `curl -X POST -d "user=a&pass=b" URL` | Sends a POST request with form data. |
| `curl -H "Header: value" URL` | Sends a custom HTTP header. |
| `curl -b "name=value" URL` | Sends a cookie with the request. |
| Burp Suite (Community) | Proxy that lets you view and modify requests between browser and server. |
| `gobuster dir -u URL -w wordlist.txt` | Guesses hidden directories from a wordlist. **Only on authorised targets**, and respect any rate limits. |

Common first checks: view page source, `/robots.txt`, cookies, comments in HTML/JS, and URL parameters.

