## 3. Cryptography & Encoding

| Command | What it does |
|---------|--------------|
| `echo "text" \| base64` | Encodes text to Base64. |
| `echo "dGV4dAo=" \| base64 -d` | Decodes Base64. |
| `echo "68656c6c6f" \| xxd -r -p` | Converts hex back into text. |
| `echo "text" \| xxd` | Shows a hex dump of data. |
| `echo "Uryyb" \| tr 'A-Za-z' 'N-ZA-Mn-za-m'` | ROT13 decode/encode (swaps each letter 13 places). |
| `md5sum file` / `sha256sum file` | Calculates a file's hash (fingerprint). |
| `openssl enc -d -aes-256-cbc -in file -out out` | Decrypts a file with OpenSSL (asks for the password). |
| CyberChef (web tool) | Drag-and-drop recipes for decoding, decrypting, and converting data. |
| `hashid <hash>` | Suggests which hash type a string might be. |

> Hash cracking tools (`john`, `hashcat`) should only be used on hashes the CTF provides, with wordlists you are allowed to use.

