## 4. Forensics

| Command | What it does |
|---------|--------------|
| `file evidence.bin` | Identifies the file type. |
| `exiftool image.jpg` | Shows metadata (author, camera, GPS, comments, software). |
| `strings -n 8 evidence.bin` | Prints text sequences of at least 8 characters. |
| `xxd evidence.bin \| head` | Shows the first bytes in hex. Useful for checking file headers ("magic bytes"). |
| `binwalk evidence.bin` | Scans a file for embedded files and data. |
| `binwalk -e evidence.bin` | Scans **and extracts** embedded files. |
| `foremost -i evidence.bin` | Carves out files by header and footer signatures. |
| Wireshark | Graphical packet analyser for `.pcap` files. Try filters like `http` or `ip.addr == x.x.x.x`. |
| `tshark -r capture.pcap -Y http` | Command-line Wireshark; `-r` reads a file, `-Y` applies a display filter. |

